  <Fragment slot="en">
    <p class="mt-6">{LEGAL.business.name} (the "Company", "we") handles the personal information of people who use {LEGAL.business.serviceName} (the "Service") under Korea's Personal Information Protection Act and related laws. This notice explains what we collect and why, how long we keep it, and who we share it with or show it to.</p>

    <h2 id="en-collect">1. What we collect, why, and how long we keep it</h2>
    <p>We collect the following directly from you in the Service or as you use it. We don't collect anything not listed here.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Information</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {COLLECTED.map((c) => <tr><td class="font-semibold">{c.cat.en}</td><td>{c.items.en}</td><td>{c.purpose.en}</td><td>{c.keep.en}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">When you delete your account, the information above is deleted immediately, and reports and admin records are unlinked from you so you can't be identified. Where a law requires us to keep something, we keep it separately for that period and then delete it. We have no payment feature, so we don't create transaction or payment records.</p>

    <h2 id="en-chat">2. Chats and when our team can see them</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only the traveler and the jigi in a request can read and write in its chat. Messages can't be edited or deleted after sending (to preserve evidence for reports).</li>
      <li><b>Our team (admins) can't read chats in general.</b> We open a conversation only when someone reports it, only as far as needed to handle the report, and every view is logged with who viewed it and when.</li>
      <li>Messages that look like they share contact details or push payment outside YEONON are detected automatically and a safety notice is shown. The message is only marked, not blocked or deleted.</li>
      <li>If you don't read a message for a while (10 minutes by default), we may email you a reminder. The email never includes the message text.</li>
      <li>Retention: deleted automatically {r.chatMonths} months after the meetup is completed or the booking is cancelled, declined or expires. Chats with an open report are kept until it's handled.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="en-admin">3. What admins can see</h2>
    <p>Admins see only what's needed to run the Service: the member list (name, email, role, status), jigi applications (for review and interviews), route reviews, bookings (to step in, e.g. force-cancel), reports and reported chats, reviews flagged for safety, recommendation logs (without showing who made them) and the waitlist. Admin actions — suspensions, reviews, report handling, viewing reported chats and exporting lists — are all logged. Sensitive fields like contact details are only exported when an admin explicitly chooses to include them.</p>

    <h2 id="en-ai">4. How we use AI</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Recommendations</b>: AI helps rank routes and write the "Why this fits you" text. We send the AI provider <b>only your preferences (interests, dates, time of day, group size, languages, vibe and your note, with emails, phone numbers and links removed) and public route information</b> (title, summary, tags, stop descriptions).</li>
      <li><b>Similarity</b>: the same kind of text is turned into number vectors (embeddings) to measure how close a route is to your taste.</li>
      <li><b>Translation</b>: only when <b>you tap Translate</b> under a chat message do we send that message to the AI provider. Translations are not stored.</li>
      <li>We <b>never send AI providers personal identifiers</b> such as your name, email, phone number or nationality. AI output is for reference only and may be wrong. If AI fails, we recommend routes by score without it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="en-processors">5. Service providers and international transfers</h2>
    <p>We use the providers below to run the Service. They are located outside Korea (mostly in the USA), so your information may be transferred abroad over the network when you use the Service. If you don't want this, you can stop using the Service and delete your account, but you won't be able to use the Service.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Country</th><th>Information</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Retention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {LEGAL.processors.map((p) => <tr><td class="font-semibold">{p.name}</td><td>{p.countryEn}</td><td>{p.itemsEn}</td><td>{p.purposeEn}</td><td>{legalValue(p.retentionEn, 'en')}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>We use the email provider (Resend) only when email notifications are turned on. The embedding provider may change with our settings; we'll update this table if it does.</p>

    <h2 id="en-share">6. What other members see, and third parties</h2>
    <p>We don't sell or give your personal information to third parties, except when required by law. Because of how the Service works, the person you're matched with sees only the following.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Travelers → their jigi</b>: display name, requested route, time and group size, request note, chat messages (jigis' reviews of travelers are not shown)</li>
      <li><b>Jigis → travelers and visitors</b>: before confirmation, part of the display name (e.g. K**), headline, bio, languages, rating and reviews, routes and open times / once confirmed, the full display name</li>
      <li><b>Public reviews</b>: travelers' reviews of jigis show the rating, text and month, with the writer's first initial only. Safety flags are never public</li>
      <li><b>Never shown</b>: email, phone number, jigi application details, a traveler's nationality and interests, profile photos, and whether someone blocked you</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="en-rights">7. Your rights</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You can ask to see, correct or delete your information, or stop its processing, at any time. You can edit your profile yourself and withdraw marketing email consent at any time.</li>
      <li><b>Delete your account</b> from your account page — it takes effect immediately and cancels open bookings.</li>
      <li>For anything else, email our privacy officer and we'll handle it without delay and let you know.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="en-age">8. Under 18s</h2>
    <p>You must be 18 or older to use the Service, and we don't collect information from children under 14. If we learn that someone under 18 has signed up, we'll suspend the account and delete their information.</p>

    <h2 id="en-cookies">9. Cookies</h2>
    <p>We use only a session cookie to keep you signed in and a temporary security cookie during sign-in. We don't use advertising or analytics cookies or tools. You can block cookies in your browser, but then you can't use features that need sign-in.</p>

    <h2 id="en-security">10. How we protect your information</h2>
    <p>All traffic is encrypted (HTTPS). Every database table has access rules (row-level security) so only you and authorized people can read it. Server keys are never exposed to browsers, admin access is kept to a minimum, and admin actions are logged.</p>

    <h2 id="en-officer">11. Privacy officer and contact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Privacy officer: {legalValue(o.name, 'en')} ({legalValue(o.title, 'en')})</li>
      <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${o.email}`}>{o.email}</a> · Phone: {legalValue(o.phone, 'en')}</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For help with a privacy concern you can also contact the Personal Information Dispute Mediation Committee (+82-1833-6972, www.kopico.go.kr) or the Personal Information Infringement Report Center (118, privacy.kisa.or.kr).</p>

    <h2 id="en-history">12. Effective date and changes</h2>
    <p>This notice takes effect on {legalDate(LEGAL.privacyVersion, 'en')}. If it changes, we'll announce it at least 7 days in advance (30 days for important changes) and ask signed-in members to agree again.</p>
